      "writtenOn": "2025-03-05T06:44:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Currently, when SCO management refactor is enabled, \n\n* `connectAudio()` to call `AudioManager#setCommunicationDevice()` to trigger an audio HAL callback in `IBluetoothAudioPort#startStream()` that will connect SCO in the stack\n\n* `disconnectAudio()` to call `AudioManager#clearCommunicationDevice()` to trigger an audio HAL callback in `IBluetoothAudioPort#stopStream()` that will disconnect SCO in the stack\n\nI think we should instrument `IBluetoothAudioPort#startStream()` and `IBluetoothAudioPort#stopStream()` as well. \n\nMoreover, when the audio HAL operation is done, HFP native stack needs to call `IBluetoothAudioProvider#streamStarted()` to indicate SCO onnection is successful, we should instrument this as well",
      "parentUuid": "89c82c91_43f42dc8",
      "revId": "c501862fdbee74c41163fb3ff36863f69455c126",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
